# HakiOS fragment: the Xiaomi Mi A2 (jasmine_sprout, devices/jasmine_sprout) -- what is true of this phone and of no other with the same SoC.
#
# Every driver of the reference phone is left out of the kernel: their addresses, pins and rails are the phone they were
# written for, and a driver of another phone touching this one is the last thing wanted. What is left in is what is written
# for this phone, and what the SDM660 family brings (soc/configs/sdm660.config).
#
# NOT YET WRITTEN FOR THIS PHONE, and therefore left out as well (docs/port-notes.md has each one and what it needs):
#   touch   the screen of this phone is a Synaptics TCM (or a Novatek NVT) on I2C1 at 0x20 (or 0x62), not a Goodix on SPI
#   storage this phone has eMMC (SDHC1 at 0x0c0c4000), not UFS
#   gpu     the Adreno 512 of this chip is not the Adreno 642L the driver was written for
#   audio   the sound of this phone is the PMIC's own codec and the SoundWire, not the reference phone's amplifiers
#   buttons the keys of this phone are the PMIC's PON inputs, not the reference phone's GPIOs
#   haptic  the motor of this phone is the PMIC's own ERM driver, not an I2C chip
#   wifi    this phone's radio is a WCN3990, not the WCN6750
#   modem   this chip's IPC is the glink transport, not the IPCC
#
# What is left in: the driver of the buttons is written for the PMIC's PON inputs of the SDM660 family (CONFIG_HAKIOS_BUTTONS
# is left out below because the driver still carries the reference phone's SPMI arbiter addresses: see docs/port-notes.md).
CONFIG_DEVICE="jasmine_sprout"

# The arguments the common configuration turns on, whose drivers are left out: an argument that only a
# driver reads, with that driver not built, is a mistake the configuration's check refuses.
# CONFIG_TOUCHSCREEN is not set
# CONFIG_GPU is not set
# CONFIG_ADSP is not set
# CONFIG_SOUND is not set
# CONFIG_WIFI is not set
# CONFIG_MODEM is not set
# CONFIG_MODEM_AGAIN is not set

# The storage: the loader offers the phone's storage as a block service (ufs=2), and it can only do that
# for a UFS. This phone has an eMMC, which no reader of the loader knows yet (docs/plan.md, stage 5.7), so
# the kernel is given no storage to begin with: a block service that read nothing would be worse.
# CONFIG_UFS is not set

# The reference phone's drivers, left out: this phone has none of their hardware.
# CONFIG_HAKIOS_GOODIX is not set
# CONFIG_HAKIOS_UFS is not set
# CONFIG_HAKIOS_ADRENO is not set
# CONFIG_HAKIOS_BT is not set
# CONFIG_HAKIOS_WIFI is not set
# CONFIG_HAKIOS_QMI is not set
# CONFIG_HAKIOS_MODEM is not set
# CONFIG_HAKIOS_ADSP is not set
# CONFIG_HAKIOS_SPEAKER is not set
# CONFIG_HAKIOS_SOUND is not set
# CONFIG_HAKIOS_MIC is not set
# CONFIG_HAKIOS_BATTERY is not set
# CONFIG_HAKIOS_HAPTIC is not set
# CONFIG_HAKIOS_CAMERA is not set
# CONFIG_HAKIOS_TORCH is not set
# CONFIG_HAKIOS_BUTTONS is not set
